# Data layer

## Server state is not component state

Never hand-roll `useState` + `useEffect` + loading + error in each screen. That
pattern has no shared cache, refetches on every mount, and races when two screens
want the same rows. Server data belongs in a query cache (TanStack Query) keyed
by entity.

## Rules

- One module per entity under `src/data/`, exporting typed functions. Screens
  import hooks from it, never the Supabase client.
- Types come from `npm run db:types`. Never hand-edit `database.types.ts`; a
  hand-written version means TypeScript is lying about the database.
- Mutations the user is watching apply optimistically and roll back on error.
- Anything requiring a secret runs in an edge function. Everything shipped in the
  app binary is public — including every `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` value.
